  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "Owners in North America who want **brand affiliation** but want to preserve more **hotel individuality** commonly look at **soft brands** and other *lifestyle/boutique-affiliated* brands.[1][6][8]\n\nThe brands most often cited in this category include:\n\n- **Autograph Collection** by Marriott[1]\n- **Curio Collection** by Hilton[1]\n- **Ascend Hotel Collection** by Choice Hotels[1][6][8]\n- **OE Collection** by Loews Hotels & Resorts[1]\n- **Radisson Individuals** by Choice Hotels/Radisson-branded portfolio in the Americas[6][8]\n- **Vignette Collection** by IHG[17]\n- **Kimpton**, **Hotel Indigo**, and **voco** are also commonly grouped among more distinctive, personality-driven IHG brands.[9][16][17]\n- **Canopy by Hilton**, **Tempo by Hilton**, and **Moxy** are similarly positioned as more characterful, design-forward options within their parent portfolios.[9][16]\n\nFor the specific idea of preserving the hotel’s own identity, the clearest examples are **Ascend Hotel Collection**, **Autograph Collection**, **Curio Collection**, and **Radisson Individuals**, since these are explicitly described as brands that let the property retain its unique name, character, or boutique feel while benefiting from the larger company’s distribution and marketing power.[1][6][8]",
